          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "These tiny babies arrive into the world with expectations of a great life, but unfortunately they have challenges ahead. Most neonates are vulnerable and need some form of resuscitation support. To improve practitioner skills in supporting neonatal care, 15 doctors and nurses from the secondary hospitals of Aga Khan University - Garden, Karimabad, Kharadar, and Hyderabad - attended an NRP workshop in CIME and practiced situations that in real life often have serious consequences if not performed competently.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
